      "problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{3{x}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can just take the constant factor out of the integral, and then apply the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{3{x}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int {x}^{-6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (\\frac{{x}^{-6+1}}{-6+1})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (\\frac{{x}^{-5}}{-5})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{15}\\cdot {x}^{-5}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{15{x}^{5}}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
